{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
  "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Appellants",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has never uncovered judicially manageable standards for determining when politicians have acted too politically in drawing district lines. Plaintiff's social science metrics composed of statewide vote to seat ratios and hypothetical projections do not solve any of these problems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Okay. But what are the questions -- you know, I need two years or two cycles worth of data. I need an S curve of a certain shape and size. I need an efficiency gap of something. What are the numbers, what are the criteria we'd have to fill in as a constitutional matter in order for a state to be able to administer this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: In Wisconsin, before this plan, was it the case that when it was something like 49 out of 99 districts were uncontested, nobody -- the election was -\u00ad wasn't contested because the one party or the other was going to win."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I have to say that I don't think you ever answered the question: If the state has a law or a constitutional amendment that's saying all legitimate factors must be used in a way to favor party X or party Y, is that lawful?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is that an equal protection violation or a First Amendment violation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you tell me what the value is to democracy from political gerrymandering? How -- how does that help our system of government?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0001-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF PAUL M. SMITH ON BEHALF OF APPELLEES"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Appellees",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SMITH: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: What the state is asking for here is a free pass to continue using an assembly map that is so extreme that it effectively nullifies democracy. As this case illustrates, it's now possible even in a 50/50 state like Wisconsin to draw a district map that is so reliably and extremely biased that it effectively decides in advance who's going to control the legislative body for the entire decade."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Why -- why is it de minimis? It seems to me it's exactly the same thing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: In a one-person one-vote case, does one person in an overpopulated district have standing to challenge not only that district, those district lines, but the entire state map?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McGhee",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. McGhee's own amicus brief outlines numerous unanswered questions with -- with this theory."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Smith",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Vieth, the Court appropriately laid down a challenge and said if you want us to do this, you've got to give us a lot more than you've given us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b585cf99936df6cf2c7e507c38e1df0386b5b305cc51cff1e15117132a826a59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b585cf99936d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How is it that we are not going to create a world in which in every district somebody can come in and say: A-ha, there's been a violation of partisan symmetry; we're entitled to a redrawn map? What's the threshold? Where do you draw the line?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1161",
      "confidence": 0.0,
